      "created_at": "2016-06-09T17:59:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So I’ve had this experience a few times now.</p>\n<p>I learned that I was playing something incorrectly in the tabletop version of the game because of what happens in the video game. Has this happened to anyone else?</p>\n<p>Here’s what I discovered today.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Wager Master’s “Breaking the Rules” causes each player to draw TWO cards at the End of Turn, presumably because you haven’t played a card or used a power that turn. Even though you probably will.</li>\n<li>Also dealing with Breaking the Rules: If a card effect, such as Scholar’s “Know When to Hold Fast” or Nightmist’s “Mist-Fueled Recovery,” causes you to immediately end your turn, you get to immediately have a second turn!</li>\n</ol>\n<p>As a side-note Darkwatch Nightmist + Breaking the Rules = stack your own deck.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:47:37.820Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 10.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 15292,
      "topic_slug": "wager-master",
      "display_username": "deddragon",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
