      "id": 177665,
      "name": "Blackfang108",
      "username": "Blackfang108",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-06-09T18:09:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There was discussion of <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#1</span> recently. It's indeed surprising, but logically follows. (In general, Breaking the Rules appears to be pretty good for the heroes.)Are we sure that <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#2</span> isn't a bug?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It actually makes perfect, logical sense.</p>\n<p>Turn order normally has \"End of Turn\" last.&nbsp; Now \"End of Turn\" is first.&nbsp; So The Scholar Draws 5 cards and goes to his \"End of Turn\" phase.&nbsp; WHich is now Followed by his Power Phase.</p>",
